<div class="flatplan_body" data-flatplan-id="flatplan_body"><div><figure class="my-4 flex flex-col"><img alt="109th Running Of The Indianapolis 500" data-flatplan-id="flatplan_mainMedia" loading="lazy" width="320" height="180" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="shadow-md rounded-lg object-contain h-auto w-full flatplan_mainMedia" style="color:transparent" src="https://s.w-x.co/wxnext/img/indy-500-051626?format=auto&optimize=medium&width=1600&quality=60"><figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm leading-tight"><p>INDIANAPOLIS, INDIANA - MAY 25: Jack Harvey, driver of the #24 DRR Cusick Invst Chevrolet, leads a pack of cars during the NTT IndyCar Series109th Running Of The Indianapolis 500 at Indianapolis Motor Speedway on May 25, 2025 in Indianapolis, Indiana. (Photo by James Gilbert/Getty Images)</p><p class="m-0 text-gray-500">(Getty Images)</p></figcaption></figure><p><br></p><p>The first round of qualifying for the 110th Indianapolis 500 was rained out Saturday, leading to a busy, condensed schedule on Sunday.</p><p>Storms and showers rained out practice on Saturday morning and kept coming into the afternoon, forcing IndyCar to push all qualifying to Sunday.</p><div class="flex items-center">
        <div class="twitter-tweet twitter-tweet-rendered" style="display: flex; max-width: 550px; width: 100%; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><iframe id="twitter-widget-0" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowtransparency="true" allowfullscreen="true" title="X Post" src="cid:frame-0AE20578FECC7B6A8B7E72EEF30BED0A@mhtml.blink" style="position: static; visibility: visible; width: 550px; height: 873px; display: block; flex-grow: 1;" data-tweet-id="2055735182292828440"></iframe></div>
      </div><p><br></p><p>Qualifying will begin at noon on Sunday, and each driver will only get one try at qualifying for the Fast 12 and a second qualifying session. More on this procedure can be found <a href="https://www.indycar.com/-/media/Files/2026/NICS/07-500/indycar-QualDraw-Sat-26I500.pdf" rel="external nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>. </p><p>Fortunately for IndyCar, Sunday's activities at Indianapolis Motor Speedway won't be rained out. Forecasters are calling for a dry, warm and mostly sunny day on Sunday.</p><figure class="my-4 flex flex-col"><img alt="Indianapolis forecast" loading="lazy" width="320" height="180" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="shadow-md rounded-lg object-contain h-auto w-full" style="color:transparent" src="https://s.w-x.co/wxnext/img/0517_INdy_Snap-f2f40c.png?format=auto&optimize=medium&width=1600&quality=60"></figure><p>The green flag will drop on the iconic race at 12:45 p.m. on May 24.</p></div></div>


